{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2155-11-01 18:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2155-11-01 18:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, thanks. I’ve had bad stomach cramps and diarrhea for about a month now. It started after I saw some sick kids and then got my IVIG infusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2155-11-01 18:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And how frequent are the stools? Any blood or fever?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2155-11-01 18:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A few times a day, liquid at first, but they’re starting to firm up. I had red stools once after red jello, but no more since. No fevers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2155-11-01 18:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that helps. Given your history of lymphoma and immune deficiency, we want to be careful. We’ll run some tests."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2155-11-01 18:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve also been feeling dizzy when I stand up. Started a few days ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2155-11-01 18:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure was low in clinic—94 over 55. That could explain the dizziness. We’ll monitor that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2155-11-01 18:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my left shoulder’s been hurting for about a week. Was I supposed to get an X-ray before coming in?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2155-11-01 18:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but it wasn’t done. We’ll order that tomorrow so we can check it out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2155-11-01 18:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I’m just worried it’s something serious with my lymphoma coming back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2155-11-01 18:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But your symptoms are more likely due to an infection, especially since others around you were sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2155-11-01 18:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I’ve been trying to eat more carbs to firm up my stools, but it’s just made my blood sugar worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2155-11-01 18:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we saw your HbA1c is 7%, so diabetes is under reasonable control. We’ll hold your metformin for now and use insulin as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2155-11-01 18:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. What about my IVIG? I’m due for it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2155-11-01 18:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give it during your stay. It’s important for your immune deficiency. We’ll also start antibiotics just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2155-11-01 18:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m allergic to penicillin and sulfa drugs. Just so you know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2155-11-01 18:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Noted. You already got cefepime and flagyl in clinic, which are safe for you. We’ll continue that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2155-11-02 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your CT scan from yesterday didn’t show any new masses or bowel issues. Lymph nodes are stable, and your spleen is slightly larger but unchanged from before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2155-11-02 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So nothing’s blocking or inflamed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2155-11-02 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, the scan looks clear. That’s reassuring. Your shoulder X-ray is also normal—no fracture or arthritis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2155-11-02 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So why does it hurt? Could it be lymphoma?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2155-11-02 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s possible, but unlikely. We’ll keep an eye on it. You may need an MRI later if it doesn’t improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2155-11-02 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief. How’s my blood work?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2155-11-02 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your white count is low—2.2—because of your immune condition. Hemoglobin is a bit low too, but stable. Platelets are okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2155-11-02 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I be worried about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2155-11-02 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not acutely. Your levels are consistent with your history. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2155-11-03 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re scheduling your colonoscopy for today. It’s mostly to rule out infection or inflammation since your symptoms haven’t fully resolved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2155-11-03 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will they take biopsies?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2155-11-03 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they’ll take a few samples. It might help us find a cause if it’s not just a virus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2155-11-03 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my IVIG? Is that still happening?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2155-11-03 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, right after the colonoscopy. You’re getting your full dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2155-11-03 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The colonoscopy was unremarkable. The inside of your bowel looks healthy. No ulcers, masses, or active inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2155-11-03 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No sign of lymphoma?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2155-11-03 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No visible signs. Biopsies are pending, but so far, nothing concerning. We also tested for C. diff and parasites—both negative."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2155-11-03 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the CMV test?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2155-11-03 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "CMV came back negative. So it’s not that either."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2155-11-03 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s causing this?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2155-11-03 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most likely a lingering viral or bacterial gastroenteritis. Your immune deficiency makes it harder to clear infections quickly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2155-11-03 14:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the antibiotics will help?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2155-11-03 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, cipro and flagyl cover a broad range of bacteria. We’ll send you home with a full course."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2155-11-03 14:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2155-11-03 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s improved, right? We think it was due to dehydration from diarrhea. Your blood pressure is still low but stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2155-11-03 14:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I feel less lightheaded now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2155-11-03 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep an eye on it. Your ostomy site looks better too—less red than when you came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2155-11-04 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. We’re planning to discharge you today. You’re feeling better, stools are firmer, and no new issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2155-11-04 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What meds am I going home with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2155-11-04 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All your usual meds, plus cipro and flagyl for a week. Also, loperamide for diarrhea and dicyclomine for cramps if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2155-11-04 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the Dilaudid? I know it’s limited."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2155-11-04 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 18 tablets. Please discuss with your pain doctor about long-term use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2155-11-04 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Any follow-up tests?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2155-11-04 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We ordered a strongyloides IgG test—important for someone on IVIG. And please follow up on the colonoscopy biopsies."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2155-11-04 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my shoulder?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2155-11-04 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If it doesn’t get better, your doctor may order an MRI. But for now, it’s likely musculoskeletal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2155-11-04 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. When should I call the doctor?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2155-11-04 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you develop fever, worsening pain, more diarrhea, or blood in stool—call right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2155-11-04 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my diabetes? Should I restart metformin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2155-11-04 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you can restart it tomorrow. Just monitor your sugars closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2155-11-04 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2155-11-04 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. You should be out by noon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2155-11-04 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check before you leave. Any new symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2155-11-04 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, all good. Stomach feels better, and I’m not dizzy anymore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2155-11-04 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Remember to follow up with your primary doctor in a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2155-11-04 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2155-11-04 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Feel better soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2155-11-01 18:10:00",
    "admission_end": "2155-11-04 19:22:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for evaluation of chronic abdominal pain and diarrhea lasting one month, in the context of multiple comorbidities including common variable immunodeficiency, large cell lymphoma in remission, and colostomy status. She also reported orthostatic dizziness and new left shoulder pain. Workup included a CT abdomen and pelvis showing stable retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy and no acute abdominal findings, a normal shoulder X-ray, and a colonoscopy with unremarkable findings and pending biopsies. Stool studies were negative for C. diff, parasites, and CMV. She was treated with intravenous antibiotics initiated in clinic and continued on ciprofloxacin and metronidazole, along with loperamide and dicyclomine for symptom control. Her symptoms improved during the hospitalization, dizziness resolved, and she was discharged home on a full course of oral antibiotics and updated symptom management medications. Follow-up was arranged for shoulder pain if persistent, strongyloides IgG results, and colonoscopy biopsies.",
    "problems": [
      "Intestinal infection due to other organism, not elsewhere classified",
      "Other malignant lymphomas, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Common variable immunodeficiency",
